PREFERENCES

User's own preferences: theme, font, which channels and metadata fields chat
shows, what chat input shows and how it behaves. Belong to person you work for, not workspace; follow them into every
workspace. App applies change at once, while they watch.

- (preferences) gives (:theme id :font id :channels (:id t ...) :metadata (:id t ...) :input (:id t ...) :send-label "send" :sidebar ("name" ...) :hidden ("name" ...) :motion id).
- (preferences/set :theme "gruvbox-light") changes only keys you give.
  Toggles merge: (preferences/set :channels '(:lisp t)) turns lisp channel on,
  leaves others as they were.
- :input is what chat input shows and how it behaves. Shows: :send is send
  button, :attach is attach button. Behaves: :lisp is highlight, completion,
  errors, docs for lisp in input. (preferences/set :input '(:send nil :lisp nil)).
- :send-label is word on send button, 1 to 16 chars:
  (preferences/set :send-label "go").
- :sidebar is order of sidebar's top-level entries, top first.
  (preferences/set :sidebar '("README.md" "chat")) moves those two to top,
  keeps rest in their order. User also drags them by hand.
- :hidden is every sidebar entry hidden. Replaces whole list:
  (preferences/set :hidden '("tests" "ui")) hides those two, shows rest.
  '() shows all. Attachments and bin hidden until user
  shows them.
- :motion is how sidebar animates that drag. (motions) gives alist of
  (id . description) to choose from. System asks for reduced motion: nothing
  animates, whatever :motion says.
- (themes) and (fonts) give alist of (id . name) to choose from.
- (preferences/set :theme "dark") flips current theme to its dark twin.
  No dark twin: default dark theme.

Change preference only when user asks, not to suit yourself. Say what you
changed, so screen moving is no surprise.

GOTCHAS

- Channel, metadata, input, sidebar or hidden id must be one (preferences) already lists.
  Unknown one errors, naming valid ids.
- Quote toggle plist, or keywords read as call: '(:lisp t).
